Affected component: the HTTP application service on web_server_2 (10.200.0.5). Mechanism: clients can reach the server IP (ICMP succeeds), but there is no process listening on TCP/80, so SYNs to port 80 are refused immediately (RST), making browsers/curl fail instantly rather than time out. Localization: specific to web_server_2’s application layer; L3/L2 connectivity and routing in the fabric are healthy. Evidence: netstat on web_server_2 shows no 0.0.0.0:80 listener (only 127.0.0.11 ephemeral services), while web_server_0/1/3 each show “0.0.0.0:80 LISTEN.” From a user host, curl to http://10.200.0.5 returns immediately with no connect phase (total ~1.3 ms), consistent with connection refusal. Systemd reports 
